      ],
      "source": "https://encyclopediaofalabama.org/article/bon-air/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A Norfolk Southern rail line still runs through Bon Air, echoing its early industrial roots.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://encyclopediaofalabama.org/article/bon-air/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The original mill built 70 houses and duplexes for workers, many of which still stand today.",
